cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ctdl-validate-jvm, please cite it as below."
title: "ctdl-validate-jvm: a JVM port of the ctdl-validate rule core, reconciled by a cross-language parity test"
abstract: >-
  A Java reimplementation of the rule core of ChelseaKR/ctdl-validate: CTID
  grammar, identifier kinds, in-payload reference resolution, domain and range
  validation with subclass closure, and inverse consistency over CTDL and
  CTDL-ASN JSON-LD payloads. Both implementations are tested against one shared
  fixture corpus and must agree finding for finding, with disagreement a build
  failure. Every finding cites the published rule it came from, with the spec
  text and its retrieval date. Deterministic, with no network calls and no model
  calls. A demonstration and reference port, not a released artifact.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chelsea
    family-names: Kelly-Reif
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChelseaKR/ctdl-validate-jvm"
url: "https://github.com/ChelseaKR/ctdl-validate-jvm"
references:
